# SQLx compile-time verification configuration
# 
# This file tells SQLx to perform compile-time verification of all SQL queries
# against the PostgreSQL database. This ensures:
# 
# 1. All queries are syntactically correct
# 2. All parameter types match column types
# 3. All referenced tables and columns exist
# 4. No SQL injection vulnerabilities can be introduced via parameterization
#
# To enable compile-time verification:
# 1. Ensure DATABASE_URL is set in your environment
# 2. Run: cargo check
#
# For CI/CD in offline mode:
# 1. Generate offline metadata: cargo sqlx prepare
# 2. Commit .sqlx/query-*.json files
# 3. Run CI with SQLX_OFFLINE=true
#
# This configuration file is a marker for SQLx. The actual verification
# happens automatically when using sqlx::query!() and sqlx::query_as!()
# macros in code.
